-WimFile "I:\images\Win11_Enterprise.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "I:\configs\unattend.xml" -DataDiskNumber 1 -EnableBitLocker -BitLockerPin "ReplaceWithYourPin42" -Force -Silent

:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
:: deploy.args — startnet.cmd's `set /p` reads ONLY the literal first line
:: above and passes it verbatim to unified_winpe_deploy.ps1. Everything in
:: this section (`::` prefix) is reference material that set /p never sees.
:: See docs/DEPLOY_ARGS.md for the full parameter reference.
::
:: The active first line is the README's canonical two-partition USB scenario:
:: legacy FAT32 WinPE boot + NTFS IMAGES data partition (I: assumed). Replace
:: -BitLockerPin "ReplaceWithYourPin42" with your real PIN before deploying.
:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
::
:: To switch scenarios, REPLACE the first line of this file with the args
:: below the matching `:: Scenario:` heading (and remove its leading `::`).
::
:: Scenario: Single-ISO workflow (build_iso.ps1 output, Rufus to USB).
:: {DRIVE} is substituted at boot time with the actual letter WinPE assigns
:: the USB, so paths stay correct regardless of enumeration order.
::   -WimFile "{DRIVE}\images\Win11_Pro_Custom.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "{DRIVE}\configs\unattend.xml" -Force -Silent
::
:: Scenario: Interactive TUI variant — pre-locates the WIM dir but still
:: prompts the operator for edition, target disk, and confirmations. Good
:: for lab / testing USBs.
::   -ImagePath "{DRIVE}\images"
